<title>CHINA: China's Jiangsu summer grain harvest seen record.</title>
<headline>China's Jiangsu summer grain harvest seen record.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's eastern Jiangsu province is expected to produce a record summer grain harvest of about 12.24 million tonnes, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>That marked an increase of 230,000 tonnes from last year, with a per hectare yield of 4,500 kg, it said, quoting the provincial Agriculture and Forestry Department.</p>
<p>The department attributed the rise to an increased area under grain, up by nearly 34,000 hectares to about 2.72 million hectares, it said.</p>
